tions. No previous programming experience required.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring, Summer&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">CSE 115LLR</span><span class=\"box-title\">Introduction to Computer Science I</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">14 or 15 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-fall\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 2</span><span class=\"col-term\">Fall</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"geographic-information-science-bs__box-2-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/pathways.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Pathway</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"geographic-information-science-bs__box-2-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/pathways.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Pathway</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"geographic-information-science-bs__box-2-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Univariate Statistics in Geography&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Introduces probability as a measure of uncertainty. Addresses the use of such measures of uncertainty for describing data, and for making inferences about large populations from small samples. These descriptive and inferential aspects of statistics are illustrated using geographic examples from a wide variety of different fields.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: true}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">GEO 211LLB</span><span class=\"box-title\">Univariate Statistics in Geography</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"geographic-information-science-bs__box-2-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Survey of Calculus and Its Applications I&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;For students in social, biological, and management sciences. Limits, continuity, differentiation of algebraic and exponential functions; applications; introduces integration.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring, Summer, Winter&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: Score of 70/100 or better on both the Fundamentals and the Algebra portions of the Math Readiness Assessment, or a C or better in ULC 148 , MTH 108 , MTH 113 , MTH 114 , MTH 115 , a D or better in MTH 121 or MTH 131 or MTH 141 or a score of 3 on AP Calculus or a score of 4 or 5 on AP Pre-Calculus.&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: true, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: true, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8036&amp;returnto=1177&quot;, &quot;groups&quot;: [{&quot;requirement_type&quot;: &quot;choice_required&quot;, &quot;group&quot;: &quot;Two Introductory Courses (choose 1 of 2)&quot;, &quot;courses&quot;: [{&quot;code&quot;: &quot;MTH 121LR&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Survey of Calculus and Its Applications I&quot;}, {&quot;code&quot;: &quot;MTH 141LR&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;College Calculus I&quot;}]}]}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">full list on click</span><span class=\"box-eyebrow-sep\"> &middot; </span><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Two Introductory Courses (choose 1 of 2)</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">14 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-spring\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 2</span><span class=\"col-term\">Spring</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"geographic-information-science-bs__box-3-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;